                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "4. Volume volatility’s negative coefficient higher std(V_t) proxies for a higher noise-trading variance  $ \\sigma_u^2 $ relative to a roughly stable  $ \\Sigma_0 $, which, by Proposition 1, lowers  $ \\lambda $ and degrades the precision of price discovery. This is consistent with the documented negative effect on subsequent returns.",
